Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.10,Header,,0,0,0,,This is a Gentlemen of the Hàn free fansub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.38,0:00:05.58,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1100,4100,5180)\pos(653.755,415.455)}Episode 57\N\N\N\N\NTaking Hànzhōng by Wit
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.03,0:00:16.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,At the battle of Mount Dingjun,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.22,0:00:19.42,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Elder General Huang Zhong, \Nat almost seventy years of age,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.42,0:00:21.81,Thinking,,0,0,0,,never declined in wisdom or bravery.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.81,0:00:27.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He cut down Xiahou Yuan \Nand took over the Wei camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.02,0:00:31.39,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Defeated, Zhang He fled back\N to Nanzheng to report to Cao Cao.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.62,0:00:34.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.70,0:00:38.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,3900,4220)\pos(1009.091,471.818)}Zhāng Hé
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.42,0:00:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhang!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.12,0:00:40.01,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Mount Dingjun is lost!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.48,0:00:47.16,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General Xiahou Yuan was\N slain by the blade of Huang Zhong!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.74,0:00:52.58,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,4500,4820)\pos(326.667,472)}Cáo Cāo\NStyled: Mèngdé
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.48,0:01:07.10,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhang!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.74,0:01:08.50,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,4500,4820)\pos(320,485.333)}Liú Yè\NStyled: Zǐyáng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.72,0:01:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall lead the royal army\N myself to avenge General Xiahou!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.12,0:01:27.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Assembled generals,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.02,0:01:31.87,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Cao Cao is leading a great army of\N 200,000 soldiers to avenge Xiahou Yuan.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.87,0:01:35.05,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Zhang He is moving\N provisions from Mount Micang
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.05,0:01:38.40,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,to the foot of the northern mountain around the Han river.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.40,0:01:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Should one infiltrate their territory, burn their provisions, and take their supplies,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.16,0:01:46.70,Default,,0,0,0,,the momentum of \NCao Cao would be broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.44,0:01:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish to take this task.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.42,0:01:51.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(892,480)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.62,0:01:55.46,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,2877,2820)\pos(335.667,482.667)}Huáng Zhōng\NStyled: Hánshēng
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.87,0:01:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,He has fought hard for too long. I'll go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.39,0:01:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I believe it is not that hard.\NBest that I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.55,0:01:59.05,Default,,0,0,0,,No, better if I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.62,0:02:01.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(332,458.667)}Liú Bèi\NStyled: Xuándé
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.04,0:02:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Generals, no need to fight one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.50,0:02:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You can go together and \Nsee who makes an achievement first.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.78,0:02:08.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,3900,4300)\pos(323.333,525.333)}Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.06,0:02:27.04,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The seizure of provisions\N is no trivial matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.04,0:02:29.48,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,General Huang, do you \Nhave any good ideas?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.48,0:02:32.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me first scout ahead,\N and then we will see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.12,0:02:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,No, let me go first.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.47,0:02:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No. I will go first.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.63,0:02:37.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I will go first!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.05,0:02:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the main general and you are only a secondary one. Why fight to be first?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.96,0:02:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,We both serve a lord. \NWhy make a fuss?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.40,0:02:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us draw lots \Nto see who goes first. Well?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.73,0:02:50.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No no no no.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.82,0:02:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I go first then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.54,0:03:00.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine then. Let us draw lots.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.70,0:03:20.24,Default,,0,0,0,,General Huang, please draw.\N Whoever draws the stone goes first.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.77,0:03:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I pick this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.74,0:03:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Well? I was supposed \Nto go first anyways!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.83,0:03:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Since you are going first, I will assist.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.22,0:03:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The northern mountain is not too far. \NWe can decide on a time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.44,0:03:56.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.77,0:04:01.26,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,The deadline can be the {\i1}wǔ{\i0} hour the\N next day. If you return before then,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.77,0:04:01.26,Note (Potential style?),NTP,0,0,0,,Note: 11 AM-1 PM
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.26,0:04:02.67,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I will stay with my unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.67,0:04:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,If you do not return, I will\N lead my troops to your aid.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.00,0:04:10.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, I will heed you. The deadline \Nwill be the {\i1}wǔ{\i0} hour the next day.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.98,0:04:11.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.47,0:04:27.40,Default,,0,0,0,,General, it is almost time. \NShould the troops be dispatched?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.40,0:04:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,We will wait longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.82,0:04:43.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Halt!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.98,0:04:48.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Huang Zhong, you old man,\N let me see if you can escape!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.76,0:04:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-General Zhao! \N-Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.00,0:05:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,General Huang is besieged! \NThe situation is critical!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.76,0:05:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,-General Zhang!\N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.03,0:05:07.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Defend the camp! Prepare bows and crossbows! Be careful!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.02,0:05:08.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.08,0:05:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Mount the horses!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.86,0:05:20.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Huang Zhong, you geezer, why not dismount and surrender now!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.35,0:06:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Huang, I come to aid you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.08,0:06:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that General?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.74,0:06:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhao Zilong of Changshan.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.87,0:06:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,So the hero of Changban is still here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.34,0:06:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Get on the horse, General Huang!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.16,0:06:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Help General Huang dismount now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.13,0:06:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Huang!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.33,0:06:55.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General Huang!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.32,0:07:00.36,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zhao saved General Huang!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.36,0:07:02.60,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where is he now?\N-Saving General Zhang Zhu!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.07,0:07:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder General, please rest in the tent.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.66,0:07:23.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The Cao army is on us!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.13,0:07:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, close the gates and \Nenter the watchtower for your safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.44,0:07:28.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Keep the gates open!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.04,0:07:33.30,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It was just me and my horse at\N Changban slope in Dangyang,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.30,0:07:36.11,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,yet I faced 830,000 troops\N like they were but grass.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.11,0:07:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, I have an army and generals.\N What is there to fear?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.98,0:07:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Dismantle the camp banners, do not ring the bells, and ready the archers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.48,0:07:44.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.09,0:08:17.08,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, should the camp be attacked?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.69,0:08:26.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}What may be false is real; \Nwhat may be real is false.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.20,0:08:27.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}This is a war strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.53,0:08:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Zhao Yun is displaying an empty camp,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.42,0:08:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}so there must be an ambush.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.32,0:08:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}How can such a little trick fool me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.66,0:08:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.85,0:09:18.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Had it not been for Zilong yesterday, \NGeneral Huang may not have lived.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.82,0:09:22.65,Default,,0,0,0,,The entire camp would be incapable \Nof leaving the tiger's mouth as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.04,0:09:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong is full of guts.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.49,0:09:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed, he is a general with a tiger's prowess.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.33,0:09:33.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You, sir, are correct: he is a general with a tiger's prowess.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.40,0:09:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, Strategos!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.96,0:09:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao's advancing through \NXiegu road to take the Han river.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.48,0:09:40.78,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Xu Huang is his Vanguard and \NWang Ping is his Deputy Vanguard!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.48,0:09:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, Cao Cao is powerless now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.29,0:09:54.20,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,My lord, you should make camp at the western bank.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.20,0:09:58.69,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,That being so, I would have a stratagem to take the Han river.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.96,0:10:07.18,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After Cao Cao was defeated at the northern mountain,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.18,0:10:10.27,Thinking,,0,0,0,,he led a great army\Nto take the Han river.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.05,0:10:15.92,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Vanguard Xu Huang, ignoring the bitter remonstrance of Deputy Vanguard Wang Ping,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.92,0:10:19.02,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,forced the army to cross westward over the Han river
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.02,0:10:21.28,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,and do battle with \Nthe river behind them.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.28,0:10:25.29,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He suffered defeat by the Shu generals Huang Zhong and Zhao Yun.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.29,0:10:28.62,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,He had to retreat to the\N eastern bank of the Han river
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.62,0:10:32.28,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,to stand off against \Nthe Shu army across it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.61,0:10:39.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, come look.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.58,0:10:51.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Cao Cao retreated behind the \NHan river and watches us across it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.49,0:10:57.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Should he ford the river and surprise us,\N a defense would be difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.14,0:11:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have a good strategy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.70,0:11:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I have one that can cause Cao Cao\N to retreat from the eastern bank.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.99,0:11:12.16,Default,,0,0,0,,General Zilong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.12,0:11:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.20,0:11:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Tonight, lead five hundred men, \Nbring many drums and horns,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.54,0:11:21.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}and prepare enough rations so as to lay an ambush below this mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.02,0:11:25.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}In three days, once you see a light\N from our watchtower flash thrice,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.64,0:11:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}beat the drums and sound the horns,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.32,0:11:29.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}but do not sally forth and fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.66,0:11:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.82,0:11:35.94,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,After three days, you will understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.94,0:11:39.99,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,By then, Cao Cao will have withdrawn \Nby tens of {\i1}li{\i0} and made camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.69,0:12:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat the drums and yell!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.31,0:12:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu army is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.64,0:12:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.73,0:12:58.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the Shu army?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.32,0:13:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, there is not a single man. \NThe Shu army has not come to raid us.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.56,0:13:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Command the entire camp\N to go back to the tents and rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.19,0:13:25.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.01,0:13:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,All soldiers, return to the tents and rest!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.66,0:14:02.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, hurry! The Shu army \Nis here for real! Up! Up!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.65,0:14:31.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, it appears this is \NZhuge Liang's bluffing strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.44,0:14:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He does this to disturb our army so that we remain restless.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.50,0:14:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, why not command the entire camp to sleep tight?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.78,0:14:44.70,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(299.333,464)}Xú Chǔ\NStyled: \NZhòngkāng
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.78,0:14:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,When the Shu army is heard, \Nthey can be ignored.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.50,0:14:48.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Thus...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.54,0:14:49.32,Default,,0,0,0,,How audacious!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.32,0:14:53.95,Default,,0,0,0,,You are but a servant! How dare you \Ntalk carelessly about the campaign!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.13,0:15:00.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The military expert freely uses \Nboth real and the fake tactics.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.20,0:15:02.81,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Should only one true action\N be among ten fake ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.81,0:15:04.88,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,would I not be \Ngiving myself up for dead?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.88,0:15:05.44,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.95,0:15:07.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you not leaving?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.66,0:15:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, what now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.44,0:15:16.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Command the camp \Nto change and sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.18,0:15:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.72,0:15:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.96,0:15:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,When you sleep, be sure\N to keep one eye open.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.97,0:15:27.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, is now not\N the time to beat the drums?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.21,0:15:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Do not rush! Let us give \NCao Cao more sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.81,0:15:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Being so on guard, how could \NCao Cao not fall back in three days?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.35,0:16:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,If I was the one being tortured,\N I would quit in two days, not three!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.25,0:16:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, come, come.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.17,0:16:13.46,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, the night is deep. \NPlease go back to your tent and rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.57,0:16:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Good, I will go rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.68,0:16:22.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Strategos, do not overwork yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.12,0:16:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, my Lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.17,0:16:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.96,0:16:35.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.13,0:16:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-Issue the order.\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.47,0:16:55.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu army is here! The Shu army is here!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.28,0:17:21.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Command the entire army to\N pack up and fall back by thirty {\i1}li!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.83,0:17:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.81,0:17:28.92,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang, using the\N decoy troops stratagem,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.92,0:17:33.33,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,forced Cao Cao to fall back from \Nthe eastern bank of the Han river.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.33,0:17:39.41,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He then sent Zhao Yun and\N Huang Zhong to ford the river in pursuit.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.69,0:17:43.06,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,Cao Cao wished to return to Nanzheng,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.06,0:17:48.15,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,but, to his surprise, Zhang Fei \Nand Wei Yan had seized Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.69,0:17:55.85,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He had to lead an army of more\N than 100,000 back to Yangping pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.85,0:18:00.47,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He also sent Xu Zhu to escort\N supplies to support the whole army.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.80,0:18:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, the supplies\N were stolen by Zhang Fei!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.24,0:18:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I have violated orders and sullied war\N prestige. I deserve ten thousand deaths!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.29,0:18:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhongkang, come, get up, get up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.46,0:18:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Victories and defeats\N often happen in war.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.30,0:18:27.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How can this be the fault of one person?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.39,0:18:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon, I will lead troops out of here and \Nfight in a decisive battle with Liu Bei.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.23,0:18:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Do go back to your tent to recuperate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.56,0:18:42.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.66,0:18:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Go now.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.62,0:19:01.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,4620,5100)\pos(939.333,484.667)}Xú Huǎng\NStyled: Gōngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.19,0:19:00.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lord has spent \Nhalf of his life in the army
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.22,0:19:02.69,Default,,0,0,0,,and has deep knowledge\N of military strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.40,0:19:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet, when he met Kongming at the \NHan river, he suffered multiple defeats.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.02,0:19:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, what do you \Nsuppose the reason to be?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.58,0:19:21.70,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,355,6700,7100)\pos(312,470)}Yáng Xiū\NStyled: Dézǔ
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.63,0:19:20.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, do you not trust me?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.56,0:19:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,General Gongming,\N forgive my rudeness.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.01,0:19:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Please stay.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.22,0:19:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}When it comes to military expertise,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.22,0:19:39.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11)}our lord should not be \Ninferior to Kongming.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.12,0:19:46.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}However, he is too suspicious, \Nwhich is undesirable in warfare.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.23,0:19:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}This made Kongming's strategy of \Nusing decoy troops succeed every time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.34,0:19:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}His defeat was not due to tactical error,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.41,0:19:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}but because of his temperament.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.49,0:20:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Sir, your words have enlightened me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.91,0:20:10.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11)}Why not express your \Ndisapproval right now
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.86,0:20:13.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}so that his errors can be corrected?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.50,0:20:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, please lie down and rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.15,0:21:21.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.77,0:21:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.92,0:21:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Where is Li Hu?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.15,0:21:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, Li Hu suddenly fell ill today.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.48,0:21:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,This new man is beloved by General Xu. \NHe was thus sent to guard you, my Lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.80,0:21:38.99,Default,,0,0,0,,My name is Zhang Gou.\NIt is a privilege to serve you, my Lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.17,0:21:49.74,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I like to slay people in my dreams.
Dialogue: 1,0:21:50.52,0:21:54.80,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Once I fall asleep, you \Nbetter not approach me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.80,0:21:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.88,0:22:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Was he joking or not?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.40,0:22:12.01,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I hear our lord give such orders often.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.01,0:22:16.02,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Whether or not that's true,\N I don't know either.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.36,0:22:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Why haven't I heard of that before?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.10,0:22:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not just you. I don't know either.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.10,0:22:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What were you two murmuring about?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:28.00,0:22:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,About our lord's blanket...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.46,0:22:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What about the blanket?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.99,0:22:37.52,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Are you dead men? Our lord's body is priceless.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.52,0:22:40.55,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Should he get a cold, \Ncould you bear the crime?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.99,0:22:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,How heartless!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.25,0:22:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.42,0:22:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I... my Lord... I was going to...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.67,0:23:00.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.82,0:23:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.17,0:23:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just here to bring your blanket!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.00,0:23:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, my Lord, spare me! My lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.37,0:23:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,General...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.75,0:23:39.57,Default,,0,0,0,,-My lord.\N-My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.35,0:23:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.05,0:23:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, this is...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.37,0:24:00.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Who murdered my attendant?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.92,0:24:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Could it be that I murdered him \Nwhile I was dreaming?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.33,0:24:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,He served me for three years, \Nalways being diligent and careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.15,0:24:36.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Unexpectedly, he died under my \Nsword today while I was dreaming.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.97,0:24:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What a pity! How regrettable!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.36,0:24:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Yang Xiu.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.96,0:24:56.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.63,0:24:59.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Write an order on my behalf:
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.56,0:25:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,pay his family three year's\N worth of grain and brocade
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.06,0:25:10.70,Default,,0,0,0,,and bury him well \Nwith the rites of a colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.70,0:25:11.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.96,0:25:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall do so now.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.98,0:25:31.96,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Sir, this campaign will \Nnot be over any time soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.96,0:25:35.68,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Should someone return to Xudu to fetch winter clothes for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.25,0:25:38.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait for a couple days.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.49,0:25:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How much longer will we stay here?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.46,0:25:49.33,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Our lord has long thought of withdrawal,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.33,0:25:53.71,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,but this expedition has \Ngained little while costing much.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.56,0:25:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,A withdrawal would be\N ridiculed by the Shu army.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.50,0:26:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,For this reason, he remains hesitant.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.47,0:26:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, please eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.76,0:26:30.55,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.17,0:26:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the watchword for the camp tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.06,0:26:33.18,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(305.333,466)}Xiàhóu Dūn\NStyled: Yuánràng
Dialogue: 0,0:26:41.30,0:26:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Chicken rib.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.40,0:26:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Chicken rib?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.62,0:26:48.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Chicken rib.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.15,0:26:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.05,0:26:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Master Yang,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.94,0:26:57.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lord has ordered that the \Nwatchword is "chicken rib" for tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.15,0:27:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,"Chicken rib"?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.33,0:27:07.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No need to fetch the winter clothes.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.72,0:27:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lord will withdraw soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.32,0:27:16.96,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You should pack up right now
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.96,0:27:20.76,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,lest you be unprepared when\N our lord issues the order to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.06,0:27:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.35,0:27:44.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Registrar Yang!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.76,0:27:46.97,Default,,0,0,0,,General Xiahou!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.56,0:27:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There is but one vague\N matter that I come...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:55.55,0:27:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, what is the meaning of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.40,0:28:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I am packing up so I am not unprepared by our lord's order to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.28,0:28:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Our lord is withdrawing?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.93,0:28:10.65,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you know, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.28,0:28:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I found out from tonight's watchword.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.31,0:28:18.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the matter\N that I come here for, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.65,0:28:21.34,Default,,0,0,0,,When our lord made the \N"chicken rib" watchword,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.13,0:28:24.90,Default,,0,0,0,,what did he mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.85,0:28:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}A chicken rib has no meat,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.27,0:28:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}but to discard it\N is to do away with its taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.50,0:28:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Now that an advance would be futile \Nwhile a retreat would draw ridicule,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.59,0:28:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}there is nothing better\N but to withdraw now.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.81,0:28:45.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Soon, our lord will \Nrecall the army back to court.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.83,0:28:48.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Therefore, I started \Nto pack up my belongings
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.34,0:28:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}lest I panic before the trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.24,0:28:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You truly know his intentions, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.23,0:29:34.58,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Hurry and pack up.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:34.58,0:29:36.52,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,We've met defeat after defeat\N ever since coming here.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.52,0:29:38.40,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,We've been frightened all day.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.57,0:29:44.84,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I heard that Registrar Yang has figured it out already:
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.84,0:29:46.27,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,this fight is futile.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.74,0:29:49.74,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like Master Yang was right.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:49.74,0:29:50.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.92,0:29:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.44,0:30:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Who told you to pack up?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.99,0:30:06.20,Default,,0,0,0,,General Xiahou.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:09.44,0:30:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell him to meet me in my tent at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.58,0:30:12.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.31,0:30:23.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You dare make such commands\N and disturb army morale?!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.34,0:30:27.69,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Even if I was so audacious, \NI could not make those ideas myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.69,0:30:29.30,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It was Registrar Yang Xiu!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.24,0:30:34.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He... he guessed that you \Nhave the desire to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.56,0:30:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Him again!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.40,0:30:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring Yang Xiu here now!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.68,0:30:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.41,0:31:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.70,0:31:14.80,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It was you who dared to guess that I wanted to withdraw
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.80,0:31:17.30,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and have the men \Npack their belongings?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.30,0:31:18.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.25,0:31:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Then tell me what I had in mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.57,0:31:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,A chicken rib has no meat, but to\N discard it is to do away with its taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.85,0:31:34.45,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You are making an analogy \Nbetween it and Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.45,0:31:38.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Thus, you have no desire to stay here \Nfor too long and wish to withdraw.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.20,0:31:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,You dare... you dare make lies\N and disturb army morale?!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.82,0:31:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,-Men!\N-Here!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.90,0:32:11.62,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I knew well that such \Na fate would befall me.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.07,0:32:16.37,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,I only wished it would come a bit later.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.77,0:32:23.10,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, do not linger for in Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.10,0:32:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It is better to withdraw soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.05,0:32:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,After I depart, I hope that\N you will take care of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.50,0:32:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute him!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.82,0:32:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.85,0:33:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Xiahou Dun!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.86,0:33:19.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.00,0:33:23.14,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You are a senior general! \NWhy did you believe the rumors?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.14,0:33:24.55,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,Morale has declined!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.55,0:33:25.77,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You should be executed!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.60,0:33:31.30,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.30,0:33:37.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Please quell your anger, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.45,0:33:43.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Your capital offense is waived for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.15,0:33:48.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone who dares guess my intent or murmur about withdrawal
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.02,0:33:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,shall end up like Yang Xiu!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.95,0:33:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Tomorrow is the decisive battle \Nbetween me and Liu Bei!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.30,0:34:11.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Liu Bei!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.57,0:34:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You are an ungrateful and wicked traitor against the imperial court!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:16.70,0:34:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not dismount and surrender now!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.99,0:34:23.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I am a clansman to the Han, obeying \Nan imperial edict to squash its enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.18,0:34:26.82,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,You murdered the empress, \Nmade yourself king,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.82,0:34:29.28,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,and ride in the imperial chariots!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.28,0:34:30.98,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,It is you who is the true traitor!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:31.32,0:34:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,-General Xu!\N-Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.12,0:34:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,-Get that treacherous Liu Bei!\N-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.63,0:35:04.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.69,0:35:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Chase them!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.40,0:35:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Whoever captures Liu Bei \Nbecomes lord of the Riverlands!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.85,0:35:27.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry, abandon the horses and retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.86,0:35:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.98,0:36:01.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Ring the bell to retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.66,0:36:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,My lord, we are about to capture Liu Bei alive. Why ring the bell?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.59,0:36:16.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}The Shu army is abandoning their horses and arms. Suspicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.89,0:36:19.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11\pos(640,672)}Relay my orders: withdraw at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.22,0:36:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord11}Execute anyone who takes\N the horses, arms, and clothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.18,0:36:40.80,Default,NTP,0,0,0,,We have orders: execute anyone who\N takes the horses, arms, and clothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.27,0:37:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Kill!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.85,0:37:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Chase!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:50.19,0:37:57.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After Cao Cao executed Yang Xiu, \Nhe forced his army to fight Liu Bei.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.02,0:38:02.81,Thinking,,0,0,0,,As anticipated by Yang Xiu, \Nhe met a terrible defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:02.81,0:38:07.69,Thinking,,0,0,0,,He had his two front teeth shot off by \NHuang Zhong and almost lost his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.60,0:38:14.11,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After Yang Xiu was killed, he received \Nan elaborate burial as a reparation.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.11,0:38:21.92,Thinking,NTP,0,0,0,,The bitter struggle for Hanzhong \Nended with the total victory of Liu Bei.

